WEBVTT

00:01:52.220 --> 00:01:56.100
What are you doing, causing explosions
right next to Sankt Porto!

00:01:56.480 --> 00:01:58.770
I only ordered you to intimidate them!

00:01:59.440 --> 00:02:02.860
We're to bring the Kashiba
Mikoshi here in the near future,

00:02:02.860 --> 00:02:04.490
yet this is how they act?

00:02:04.490 --> 00:02:08.660
It will take another hundred years
to train true soldiers, I suppose.

00:02:21.090 --> 00:02:23.960
Isn't it a bit early for
us to move the Salamandra?

00:02:23.960 --> 00:02:27.050
I want them to send out a Mobile Suit squad.

00:02:28.140 --> 00:02:30.760
- Raraiya!
- ﻿Raraiya!

00:02:30.760 --> 00:02:33.220
- Chuchumy! Chuchumy!
- ﻿Raraiya, why are you running so fast?

00:02:33.220 --> 00:02:35.810
That girl understands the situation.

00:02:35.810 --> 00:02:38.140
She's heading straight
back to the locker room.

00:02:39.360 --> 00:02:40.730
There?

00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:44.610
She even remembered the
location of her locker!

00:02:44.610 --> 00:02:45.940
Wow!

00:02:45.950 --> 00:02:47.200
Oh, thanks.

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:48.530
Raraiya.

00:02:48.530 --> 00:02:51.200
Are you aware of the
warning from Towasanga—

00:02:52.450 --> 00:02:55.540
Isn't it a little soon to talk about that?

00:02:55.540 --> 00:02:57.580
Oh, she does seem frightened.

00:02:57.580 --> 00:02:58.750
- Earlier...
- ﻿Yes?

00:02:58.750 --> 00:03:01.500
What were you speaking with
Inspector General Gusion about?

00:03:03.420 --> 00:03:05.590
What were you talking about?

00:03:05.590 --> 00:03:06.720
What do you mean?

00:03:06.720 --> 00:03:10.140
Your father said he was going
back to the Rattle-Python.

00:03:10.140 --> 00:03:13.390
The Capital Army will be
coming up in the Crown.

00:03:13.390 --> 00:03:15.270
Raraiya?

00:03:15.270 --> 00:03:16.560
You need a helmet!

00:03:16.560 --> 00:03:17.680
It's Chuchumy's!

00:03:17.690 --> 00:03:20.230
- Raraiya!
- ﻿Your helmet!

00:03:20.230 --> 00:03:21.900
Hold your horses!

00:03:21.900 --> 00:03:24.270
Hey, you look to be in high spirits.

00:03:24.900 --> 00:03:26.650
Hey, it's Kerbes!

00:03:26.650 --> 00:03:28.150
What are you doing here?

00:03:28.150 --> 00:03:31.360
I came up here to save you people, obviously!

00:03:31.370 --> 00:03:34.830
Luan brought a G-Self backpack.
He's waiting outside.

00:03:34.830 --> 00:03:37.660
Huh? Thank you!

00:03:37.960 --> 00:03:40.000
I'm impressed you were able
to bring a Recksnow in here.

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:42.710
I'm from the Capital Guard, if you'll recall.

00:03:43.170 --> 00:03:47.090
Besides, with Lieutenant Luan's
Grimoire, we can get in here.

00:03:47.090 --> 00:03:49.260
Oh! The director is here!

00:03:49.680 --> 00:03:52.220
- Are you going out?
- That's the plan.

00:03:52.550 --> 00:03:55.760
The Rattle-Python and those under
it will head out to intercept them,

00:03:55.770 --> 00:03:57.640
using the Capital Tower as a shield.

00:03:57.640 --> 00:03:59.930
Fighting a battle here is
among the worst of all taboos.

00:04:00.230 --> 00:04:01.980
A ship from our fleet was taken out.

00:04:01.980 --> 00:04:05.690
The explosion from that could
have damaged Sankt Porto.

00:04:05.690 --> 00:04:08.320
Be that as it may, war is taboo!

00:04:08.320 --> 00:04:11.450
- Mom...
- ﻿I am the Crown's operations director.

00:04:11.860 --> 00:04:14.120
You can use the Arcane, yeah?

00:04:14.120 --> 00:04:16.490
Yes, and we have everyone with us.

00:04:16.490 --> 00:04:18.290
It's His Holiness!

00:04:20.210 --> 00:04:22.790
I am sorry to cause you such worry.

00:04:22.790 --> 00:04:26.130
Your Holiness, please get aboard our boat.

00:04:26.540 --> 00:04:29.050
Inspector General Gusion and Director Wilmit,

00:04:29.050 --> 00:04:30.590
you need not concern yourselves with us.

00:04:30.930 --> 00:04:34.550
The fleet from the moon
will never bomb this place.

00:04:34.550 --> 00:04:38.640
How can you say that of people
who just blew up a warship?

00:04:38.810 --> 00:04:39.390
Their ancestors were the holy and noble
men who established the Hermes Foundation.

00:04:39.390 --> 00:04:41.060
Let's bring out the G-Self.

00:04:41.060 --> 00:04:42.270
Yeah.

00:04:42.270 --> 00:04:43.770
I'll head out as well.

00:04:43.770 --> 00:04:44.770
Are we working with the main fleet?

00:04:44.770 --> 00:04:45.480
How can you say that with such certainty?

00:04:45.480 --> 00:04:48.780
Over there, the bigwigs are
talking. And over here...

00:04:49.690 --> 00:04:51.990
Oh! They're heading out for the front.

00:04:54.910 --> 00:04:57.370
That's dangerous! Make her stop!

00:04:59.370 --> 00:05:00.950
Stop it!

00:05:00.960 --> 00:05:03.460
- Stop!
- ﻿What's going on?

00:05:03.460 --> 00:05:06.830
She says she doesn't like the
tape that's tying up the G-Self.

00:05:06.840 --> 00:05:10.050
Bellri, hurry up and get those two aboard!

00:05:10.050 --> 00:05:11.800
Oh, right.

00:05:11.800 --> 00:05:17.220
Captain Klim is saying if they take the
enemy's leader, the fleet might withdraw.

00:05:18.390 --> 00:05:20.930
Sounds like something that
Captain Genius would come up with.

00:05:20.930 --> 00:05:22.310
Good girl.

00:05:22.310 --> 00:05:25.310
Can we stop the Amerian
Army from doing that?

00:05:25.310 --> 00:05:28.980
It seems like they need to
protect the bigwigs.

00:05:28.980 --> 00:05:31.570
Head outside and install that backpack!

00:05:31.570 --> 00:05:34.070
- ﻿Roger.
- Did the Garanden head out as well?

00:05:34.740 --> 00:05:38.320
The director is using Capital
Tower's standard comms line.

00:05:38.740 --> 00:05:41.330
Where was the Garanden hiding?

00:05:41.330 --> 00:05:44.330
It seems they were in Nut #143.

00:05:44.330 --> 00:05:46.290
Inspector General Gusion!

00:05:46.290 --> 00:05:49.670
Careless actions will only serve
to agitate the fleet from the moon.

00:05:50.090 --> 00:05:52.630
I'm aware of that, but they started this.

00:05:52.630 --> 00:05:54.470
It's from the Megafauna.

00:05:54.470 --> 00:05:56.340
It's me, Captain Donyell.

00:05:57.430 --> 00:05:59.180
I read you loud and clear.

00:05:59.180 --> 00:06:02.020
What? The Garanden is heading our way?

00:06:02.020 --> 00:06:04.730
Th-They're suggesting that as fellow Earthnoids,

00:06:04.730 --> 00:06:09.270
we should put up a common front
against the mystery fleet?

00:06:09.270 --> 00:06:11.230
A common front?

00:06:11.230 --> 00:06:20.490
Emergency live now!

00:06:20.990 --> 00:06:22.660
What the heck?

00:06:35.130 --> 00:06:36.300
What's up?

00:06:37.340 --> 00:06:40.090
Dorette... Dorette...

00:06:40.100 --> 00:06:40.930
Dorette...

00:06:40.930 --> 00:06:42.850
Raraiya? What's wrong?

00:06:42.850 --> 00:06:47.560
Do... Noutu Dorette. Dorette. Do... Do...

00:06:47.560 --> 00:06:49.980
All men, stand by outside.

00:06:49.980 --> 00:06:51.310
Your Holiness!

00:06:51.690 --> 00:06:54.650
Pinning our hopes on the young, eh?

00:07:02.330 --> 00:07:05.950
There's a ship moving between
the cables of Capital Tower.

00:07:05.960 --> 00:07:09.080
Does this mean we need to put up a barrier?

00:07:09.080 --> 00:07:11.250
There's no need to do anything so rash.

00:07:11.250 --> 00:07:14.170
They've just come up to space.
They're still wet behind the ears.

00:07:15.880 --> 00:07:18.300
Luan is over there.

00:07:18.300 --> 00:07:20.010
He's with Kerbes.

00:07:20.800 --> 00:07:21.840
Here I go!

00:07:24.270 --> 00:07:29.230
Huh? Isn't that Captain Klim's ship?
The Salamandra, or whatever it's called?

00:07:29.980 --> 00:07:32.520
This is Sankt Porto!

00:07:32.520 --> 00:07:35.190
Luan, thank you.

00:07:35.190 --> 00:07:37.610
- Turn around so I can see your back.
- ﻿Sure.

00:07:39.700 --> 00:07:41.910
There's three of you stuffed in there?

00:07:42.200 --> 00:07:44.830
- You were watching us, weren't you?
- ﻿Now, listen...

00:07:44.830 --> 00:07:47.620
You may be participating in the joint front.

00:07:47.960 --> 00:07:50.080
Send Raraiya and Noredo over to me!

00:07:52.290 --> 00:07:54.460
- What do you mean by joint?
- ﻿Raraiya, what's wrong?

00:07:54.750 --> 00:07:58.170
All right, I'll swap out your battery too.

00:07:58.720 --> 00:08:00.340
General Noutu Dorette is coming here!

00:08:00.340 --> 00:08:01.630
Raraiya

00:08:01.640 --> 00:08:03.220
Noutu!

00:08:03.220 --> 00:08:05.140
Noutu! Noutu!

00:08:05.140 --> 00:08:06.600
- Do-Do-Do-Dorette!
- ﻿Raraiya!

00:08:08.310 --> 00:08:09.430
You're good to go!

00:08:09.440 --> 00:08:11.890
Lieutenant Kerbes, Bellri, I'm done.

00:08:12.350 --> 00:08:13.650
Thankee.

00:08:14.770 --> 00:08:18.320
- Then that's the Garanden?
- Right.

00:08:19.110 --> 00:08:23.030
It seems they made contact with Klim
and the others aboard the Salamandra.

00:08:23.030 --> 00:08:24.910
If there's a mystery fleet,

00:08:24.910 --> 00:08:27.200
it's the common enemy of all Earthnoids,

00:08:27.200 --> 00:08:30.040
so we'll cooperate to fight them.

00:08:30.580 --> 00:08:34.630
I heard the Capital Army bought
the Garanden from Gondwan.

00:08:34.630 --> 00:08:35.790
Chuchumy.

00:08:35.790 --> 00:08:37.500
Where did you hear that?

00:08:37.500 --> 00:08:39.210
From the XO, maybe?

00:08:39.210 --> 00:08:40.300
From someone here?

00:08:40.300 --> 00:08:41.880
All right!

00:08:42.630 --> 00:08:45.470
- Kerbes!
- ﻿The Garanden is our enemy, you know!

00:08:46.600 --> 00:08:49.390
The Recksnow is the Capital Guard's.

00:08:49.390 --> 00:08:51.810
There's no way the Capital
Army could shoot it.

00:08:51.810 --> 00:08:53.140
Here I go!

00:09:00.320 --> 00:09:02.900
There are four machines! Four!

00:09:03.950 --> 00:09:06.740
There should have been a request
from Colonel Cumpa as well.

00:09:07.080 --> 00:09:10.540
That's four Mobile Suits who may have once
been our enemies you're taking aboard.

00:09:10.540 --> 00:09:13.250
Right now, they're our fellow Earthnoids.

00:09:13.250 --> 00:09:17.380
They call it a mystery fleet,
but from what continent?

00:09:17.670 --> 00:09:19.170
Towasanga.

00:09:19.170 --> 00:09:21.880
They're from the colony
beyond the moon, I'm sure.

00:09:21.880 --> 00:09:24.260
Ridiculous! What a joke!

00:09:24.260 --> 00:09:27.350
A Gondwanese man like yourself
may have trouble believing it,

00:09:27.350 --> 00:09:31.970
but it is because of people like them
that the Garanden could be built.

00:09:33.810 --> 00:09:37.560
Here I am. Your friendly welcoming party.

00:09:38.860 --> 00:09:41.190
The remaining two of you, show me your faces.

00:09:44.240 --> 00:09:46.410
Wuxia, take up alert positions outside.

00:09:46.410 --> 00:09:48.160
Do it in shifts with the
suits that have joined us.

00:09:48.490 --> 00:09:51.700
The Barara Team will be guarding the rear.

00:09:51.700 --> 00:09:53.080
That's not what you said before!

00:09:53.870 --> 00:09:56.330
Don't underestimate the fleet from Towasanga.

00:09:56.930 --> 00:09:58.470
Ah... Yes, sir

00:09:58.470 --> 00:10:01.300
This is a chance to make our
enemies fight each other.

00:10:01.300 --> 00:10:03.920
We should test our luck only when we have to.

00:10:04.800 --> 00:10:06.380
You've grown tough.

00:10:11.560 --> 00:10:13.270
Mechanic check.

00:10:13.270 --> 00:10:14.770
Wait!

00:10:15.600 --> 00:10:16.770
Raraiya!

00:10:17.860 --> 00:10:18.980
Hey, that's right!

00:10:18.980 --> 00:10:20.980
- Chuchumy!
- ﻿Noredo!

00:10:21.900 --> 00:10:22.940
Y-Yes?

00:10:22.990 --> 00:10:26.240
It's Manny! Manny Ambassada!

00:10:26.240 --> 00:10:28.910
What are you doing here, Manny?

00:10:28.910 --> 00:10:31.240
I heard Luin left for the front.

00:10:31.240 --> 00:10:32.790
I came here to search for him!

00:10:32.790 --> 00:10:34.700
So he joined the Capital Army!

00:10:34.710 --> 00:10:35.710
Y-Yeah...

00:10:36.050 --> 00:10:37.920
Manny? It's Manny!

00:10:37.920 --> 00:10:42.210
Hey! We haven't seen each other since
the pirates attacked the Crown!

00:10:42.210 --> 00:10:44.090
Did you find Luin?

00:10:44.090 --> 00:10:45.510
No...

00:10:45.510 --> 00:10:47.470
Oh, it's Captain Mask!

00:10:47.470 --> 00:10:49.590
I know who you are.

00:10:49.600 --> 00:10:52.810
You're the pirate woman who
got captured on the Crown.

00:10:52.810 --> 00:10:55.810
And you're the one who attacked me.

00:10:56.310 --> 00:10:58.980
Treatment befitting those who
declare themself a pirate.

00:11:00.110 --> 00:11:01.770
Let's not do this.

00:11:01.770 --> 00:11:05.320
I've heard the Garanden will be
attacking the mystery fleet as well.

00:11:05.320 --> 00:11:09.410
It sounds like your Salamandra is
in the mood to cooperate as well.

00:11:09.820 --> 00:11:13.490
Captain, you must have let our
Amerian genius cajole you into this.

00:11:13.880 --> 00:11:15.490
Klim Nick, huh?

00:11:15.500 --> 00:11:18.210
Do I look like such a rash man?

00:11:18.750 --> 00:11:22.340
It seems a unit of Mobile Suits
has launched from the Salamandra.

00:11:22.340 --> 00:11:24.130
That was surprisingly quick.

00:11:24.130 --> 00:11:26.010
I am Barara Peor.

00:11:26.010 --> 00:11:28.420
It's <i>such</i> a pleasure to meet you.

00:11:28.430 --> 00:11:31.260
The Salamandra is next to Sankt Porto,

00:11:31.260 --> 00:11:32.600
and they've sent out Mobile Suits.

00:11:32.970 --> 00:11:35.140
That's an appalling violation of the taboo!

00:11:35.140 --> 00:11:36.390
Do you believe it?

00:11:36.890 --> 00:11:40.230
That the Salamandra and Garanden will
actually put up a communal front?

00:11:40.230 --> 00:11:41.730
They're serious about it.

00:11:41.730 --> 00:11:45.150
They're even looking after
our suits for us.

00:11:45.150 --> 00:11:46.280
R-Right!

00:11:46.650 --> 00:11:49.400
You want us to prepare to
launch Mobile Suits, right?

00:11:49.400 --> 00:11:51.110
S-See you later!

00:11:51.110 --> 00:11:53.240
Take care! You too Bellri!

00:11:53.700 --> 00:11:55.370
- ﻿Will do.
- Raraiya?

00:11:56.450 --> 00:11:59.830
Nobell and Chuchumy.

00:11:59.830 --> 00:12:03.460
Miss Aida, take care of
Raraiya and Noredo for me.

00:12:04.130 --> 00:12:06.300
Luan, would you come with me?

00:12:06.710 --> 00:12:09.010
I don't get chances like this often!

00:12:09.010 --> 00:12:10.340
What's up?

00:12:10.380 --> 00:12:13.590
Lieutenant, you protect
Miss Aida and the others.

00:12:13.970 --> 00:12:17.350
I'd like to go into Sankt Porto too!

00:12:17.350 --> 00:12:19.850
Chuchumy. Nobell.

00:12:21.560 --> 00:12:23.810
Sankt Porto.

00:12:32.070 --> 00:12:35.370
Okay! I'll permit the unit that's
joined us to launch as well!

00:12:40.500 --> 00:12:43.540
Lieutenant, look after Noredo and Raraiya.

00:12:43.540 --> 00:12:44.620
Sure!

00:12:44.630 --> 00:12:47.750
- Protect the Megafauna, too.
- ﻿I know!

00:12:47.750 --> 00:12:49.750
If you don't hurry and go, Mask
won't take you seriously!

00:13:02.230 --> 00:13:03.770
Light signals?

00:13:03.770 --> 00:13:06.600
That there must be Captain
Klim Nick of the Amerian Army.

00:13:08.360 --> 00:13:11.070
Yes, we call it the Blue Jahannam.

00:13:11.070 --> 00:13:12.570
Jahannam, huh?

00:13:21.330 --> 00:13:24.830
The Amerian Army has gotten all the
way inside the port at Sankt Porto.

00:13:26.080 --> 00:13:28.330
Because they have a genius
commanding them, right?

00:13:39.640 --> 00:13:42.470
I am Captain Mask of the Capital Army.

00:13:42.470 --> 00:13:45.770
I am pleased that you accepted our proposal.

00:13:45.770 --> 00:13:47.690
We are fellow Earthnoids.

00:13:47.690 --> 00:13:50.150
Does it seem we have a chance of winning?

00:13:50.150 --> 00:13:52.570
It seems the enemy fleet has
sent out a negotiating team.

00:13:52.650 --> 00:13:55.240
but if we crush the big guy
in the middle of the fleet,

00:13:55.240 --> 00:13:58.160
their soldiers, unaccustomed
to war, will scatter.

00:13:58.160 --> 00:14:00.410
Well, that's a splendid idea!

00:14:00.410 --> 00:14:02.910
Soldiers unaccustomed to war, huh?

00:14:02.910 --> 00:14:05.160
They sent out a boat to
negotiate, didn't they?

00:14:05.160 --> 00:14:07.000
Bellri, my boy, is that you?

00:14:07.000 --> 00:14:09.830
We need only pretend we never noticed it.

00:14:09.840 --> 00:14:12.130
Furthermore, we ourselves
will serve as envoys.

00:14:14.130 --> 00:14:15.590
A white flag, huh?

00:14:15.590 --> 00:14:17.380
I see.

00:14:17.380 --> 00:14:21.930
We pretend to surrender, then when
we get close, we crush their leader!

00:14:21.930 --> 00:14:23.470
No wonder they call you a genius!

00:14:23.470 --> 00:14:25.730
You got it!

00:14:25.730 --> 00:14:28.100
However, I would feel insecure
doing it all by my lonesome,

00:14:28.100 --> 00:14:30.440
so I have Mick to accompany me.

00:14:31.070 --> 00:14:33.020
I'm the Hecate's pilot, Mick Jack.

00:14:33.440 --> 00:14:35.820
Moreover, without all of you cooperating,

00:14:35.820 --> 00:14:38.030
I would never have found
the courage to do it.

00:14:38.030 --> 00:14:41.280
Barara, you know what the
Captain is thinking now?

00:14:41.280 --> 00:14:43.370
I understand <i>quite</i> well!

00:14:43.370 --> 00:14:43.870
I am Barara Peor. It's a pleasure
to be working with you.

00:14:43.870 --> 00:14:46.540
<i>﻿I'd have expected about as much
from the president's idiot son.</i>

00:14:56.260 --> 00:14:58.550
Moran Team, have you
noticed what's happening?

00:14:58.550 --> 00:15:02.930
An Earthnoid Mobile Suit unit has
gone on the move from the big pier.

00:15:09.440 --> 00:15:10.770
Say what?!

00:15:13.070 --> 00:15:14.650
A white flag?!

00:15:14.650 --> 00:15:16.530
That means they've surrendered!

00:15:17.110 --> 00:15:18.400
Colonel Turbo!

00:15:18.400 --> 00:15:21.160
An envoy of surrender is
heading for our fleet!

00:15:21.160 --> 00:15:22.160
Shall I call them back?

00:15:22.530 --> 00:15:25.700
An envoy who comes without prior
announcement is nothing but a fool.

00:15:25.700 --> 00:15:30.120
- Drive them off.
- ﻿Shoot down any who act unofficially.

00:15:30.120 --> 00:15:32.210
Yes, sir. We shall.

00:15:32.210 --> 00:15:34.630
If Minovsky Particles aren't spread,

00:15:34.630 --> 00:15:37.460
we can obliterate them in one
fell swoop with homing missiles.

00:15:44.220 --> 00:15:47.770
Wow! That's a space fleet?
What are we gonna do about it?

00:15:55.860 --> 00:15:57.070
They saw through us!

00:16:06.620 --> 00:16:09.040
The G-Self protected us?

00:16:09.040 --> 00:16:10.000
Mick!

00:16:11.370 --> 00:16:13.620
I won't let them land a direct hit!

00:16:13.630 --> 00:16:15.340
Barara! How about intercepting them?!

00:16:18.510 --> 00:16:20.590
This is the Mack Knife's specialty!

00:16:21.090 --> 00:16:22.800
Grimoires can do it too!

00:16:24.050 --> 00:16:25.430
Take this!

00:16:28.470 --> 00:16:29.970
Retreat!

00:16:31.100 --> 00:16:33.140
Bellri? What are you doing?!

00:16:33.150 --> 00:16:34.560
They've seen through the plan!

00:16:35.770 --> 00:16:37.570
- What?
- ﻿We have to retreat!

00:16:37.900 --> 00:16:41.570
The white flag has been torn up!
Follow the G-Self and the blue one!

00:16:41.570 --> 00:16:42.900
We're retreating?

00:16:55.080 --> 00:16:56.830
Wh-What?

00:16:56.840 --> 00:16:59.380
It's because Sankt Porto is right behind us.

00:16:59.380 --> 00:17:00.590
Oh.

00:17:00.590 --> 00:17:03.340
They could never fire on us like this.

00:17:06.260 --> 00:17:07.970
The battle has ended.

00:17:07.970 --> 00:17:10.810
The negotiators have entered Sankt Porto.

00:17:11.140 --> 00:17:14.520
We must protect the negotiators.

00:17:25.450 --> 00:17:30.450
His Excellency, General Noutu
Dorette has now arrived.

00:17:35.670 --> 00:17:39.000
I did not expect you to come meet
us in person, Your Holiness.

00:17:39.000 --> 00:17:42.210
SU-Cord.

00:17:42.210 --> 00:17:44.220
General Noutu Dorette,

00:17:44.220 --> 00:17:47.390
I am grateful that you have come.

00:17:47.800 --> 00:17:49.140
We'll hurry.

00:17:49.140 --> 00:17:51.390
- Noredo.
- ﻿Come on, run!

00:17:56.190 --> 00:17:57.770
Pardon me.

00:17:59.520 --> 00:18:00.860
Going up.

00:18:02.650 --> 00:18:04.190
It just turned out this way.

00:18:04.190 --> 00:18:05.820
Long time no see.

00:18:05.820 --> 00:18:07.910
Cadet Bellri Zenam?

00:18:07.910 --> 00:18:09.370
Miss Aida?!

00:18:09.370 --> 00:18:12.450
- My lady, you seem well.
- Thank you.

00:18:12.790 --> 00:18:14.830
Lieutenant Aida Surugan,

00:18:14.830 --> 00:18:18.540
I would ask you to refer to me by
my nom de guerre, Captain Mask.

00:18:18.540 --> 00:18:20.500
Captain?

00:18:20.500 --> 00:18:23.170
- This is...
- ﻿Lieutenant Barara Peor.

00:18:23.420 --> 00:18:26.010
What are your intentions here, Captain?

00:18:26.010 --> 00:18:28.130
If I see the enemy commander's face,

00:18:28.140 --> 00:18:31.050
it will help me formulate our next plan.

00:18:31.050 --> 00:18:32.350
- Right?
- I guess...

00:18:32.350 --> 00:18:33.680
Right?

00:18:38.150 --> 00:18:40.060
One card per person.

00:18:41.150 --> 00:18:43.860
You can get to the cathedral in five minutes.

00:18:45.690 --> 00:18:47.990
I don't really get it.

00:18:47.990 --> 00:18:50.490
Oh, that's the port entrance building.

00:18:50.820 --> 00:18:53.070
﻿It's obvious, if you consider
how things are structured.

00:18:53.580 --> 00:18:55.910
After you go up, you go down.

00:18:56.330 --> 00:18:58.120
The scale here is impressive.

00:18:58.120 --> 00:19:00.880
Only high class groups
are able to get in here.

00:19:01.250 --> 00:19:03.630
- Is that it?
- It must be.

00:19:08.180 --> 00:19:09.840
What's wrong?

00:19:09.840 --> 00:19:11.890
Huh? You have a fever?

00:19:11.890 --> 00:19:12.890
Take care of her.

00:19:13.220 --> 00:19:15.560
There's got to be a doctor here at least.

00:19:15.560 --> 00:19:17.770
Ask at that mansion.

00:19:17.770 --> 00:19:18.770
Huh?

00:19:19.440 --> 00:19:21.400
A doctor, huh?

00:19:21.730 --> 00:19:24.940
We have come as guards for
Inspector General Gusion.

00:19:24.940 --> 00:19:28.650
I, too, must insist you let me
inside to guard Director Wilmit.

00:19:28.650 --> 00:19:31.030
Some guards you are, arriving this late!

00:19:31.030 --> 00:19:33.160
We're doing it to match your numbers.

00:19:33.490 --> 00:19:35.120
We're going in.

00:19:35.120 --> 00:19:39.330
Recently, you Earthnoids have treated
Universal Century technology

00:19:39.330 --> 00:19:41.120
as though it were a child's toy.

00:19:42.670 --> 00:19:46.670
It is precisely because the taboo was in
place that the Earth has recovered this far.

00:19:46.670 --> 00:19:48.130
Why do you not understand that?

00:19:48.130 --> 00:19:53.550
﻿And yet your side has been
constructing﻿ a fleet to invade Earth.

00:19:53.550 --> 00:19:55.470
Over the past ten years,

00:19:55.470 --> 00:19:58.390
you Earthnoids have gone as far
as fighting intercontinental wars.

00:19:58.390 --> 00:20:01.100
When that happened, it became
apparent to General Noutu Dorette

00:20:01.100 --> 00:20:03.770
that we would require
military forces of our own.

00:20:04.400 --> 00:20:06.690
I have it all figured out!

00:20:06.690 --> 00:20:12.240
You have been tempted by Ameria's bitter
enemy Gondwan into invading Earth.

00:20:12.240 --> 00:20:13.530
And then,

00:20:13.530 --> 00:20:16.570
you will carry out a colonization
of Earth — a Reconguista!

00:20:16.580 --> 00:20:19.040
That is your true intent!

00:20:19.040 --> 00:20:20.790
You filth!

00:20:21.920 --> 00:20:23.330
You punk!

00:20:23.880 --> 00:20:25.460
Hey, you can't do that!

00:20:27.630 --> 00:20:30.720
You've only come this far because Towasanga
keeps supplying you with Photon Batteries!

00:20:30.720 --> 00:20:31.880
Towasanga?

00:20:31.880 --> 00:20:33.510
Down on Earth,

00:20:33.510 --> 00:20:36.220
you've left behind a history of weakness!

00:20:36.890 --> 00:20:38.970
You call our history weak?

00:20:38.970 --> 00:20:40.470
Well...

00:20:40.480 --> 00:20:44.400
For the reconstruction of Earth,
the passion of Towasanga is vital.

00:20:44.400 --> 00:20:46.690
Ports for fleets are vital as well.

00:20:47.150 --> 00:20:48.770
Inspector General Gusion,

00:20:48.780 --> 00:20:53.070
I would ask you to communicate this
to the president and people of Ameria.

00:20:53.700 --> 00:20:55.950
In regards to Crown operations,

00:20:55.950 --> 00:20:58.830
I would ask you to carry
on as you have, Director.

00:20:58.830 --> 00:20:59.990
Y-Yes, sir.

00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:01.410
One more thing.

00:21:01.410 --> 00:21:04.920
That Ameria managed to
construct a space fleet,

00:21:05.290 --> 00:21:09.050
means that you must have had
collaborators from Towasanga.

00:21:09.050 --> 00:21:11.590
Not just survivors of the Rayhunton family,

00:21:11.590 --> 00:21:14.220
there must have been many more stowaways.

00:21:14.220 --> 00:21:18.350
﻿I would like to put your terms
in writing. Do you object?

00:21:18.360 --> 00:21:20.140
In writing?

00:21:20.140 --> 00:21:22.480
I would request another
meeting to discuss this.

00:21:23.140 --> 00:21:25.650
- Your Holiness?
- Let it be done.

00:21:28.770 --> 00:21:30.440
Miss Aida!

00:21:32.110 --> 00:21:33.820
Is it from the colonel?

00:21:33.820 --> 00:21:35.030
Well, yeah.

00:21:35.030 --> 00:21:36.740
Hey! Hey!

00:21:36.740 --> 00:21:38.780
Raraiya said she likes that house!

00:21:38.780 --> 00:21:41.620
- Huh?
- It's right beside the doctor's place!

00:21:44.710 --> 00:21:46.830
So she didn't have a fever!

00:21:47.250 --> 00:21:49.420
He said it might have been
caused by thinking too much.

00:21:49.420 --> 00:21:51.340
Hm?

00:21:51.340 --> 00:21:53.840
Luan, you'll be able to meet
up with the Megafauna, right?

00:21:53.840 --> 00:21:55.420
Y-Yes.

00:21:55.430 --> 00:21:58.010
Tell the Megafauna we're going to Towasanga.

00:21:58.010 --> 00:22:00.470
- Have them get ready.
- ﻿What?!

00:22:00.470 --> 00:22:02.140
Seriously?!

00:22:02.140 --> 00:22:05.350
How are we to understand anything
just by listening to those people?

00:22:05.350 --> 00:22:08.980
We'll just have to go see this
Towasanga place for ourselves!

00:22:08.980 --> 00:22:12.860
D-Does that place really exist
on the far side of the moon?

00:22:13.320 --> 00:22:15.780
That's why we're going
to see it for ourselves!

00:24:01.520 --> 00:24:04.520
Manny, who we'd finally met again,
went back to the Garanden,

00:24:04.520 --> 00:24:08.770
and Klim and Mask fought a battle
using Sankt Porto as a shield,

00:24:08.940 --> 00:24:10.150
so I finally snapped!

00:24:10.860 --> 00:24:12.990
Raraiya got better.

00:24:12.990 --> 00:24:14.990
Then, as if it was just something
we'd do during the battle,

00:24:14.990 --> 00:24:17.320
Aida said we would go to the moon,

00:24:17.330 --> 00:24:19.120
trying to cajole me into it.

00:24:19.330 --> 00:24:21.450
Next time on Reconguista in G,

00:24:21.450 --> 00:24:23.460
Space and Mobile Suit Battles.

00:24:23.460 --> 00:24:25.830
Face reality!
